From 108cefbb4191dae42893f5e9e2e9fbabec3dcd4f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rui Luo <u8076655@anu.edu.au>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 03:46:42 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] Build on Linux against faiss 5702caf; refinement
 benchmark (reference mode)

Compile fixes only, the same ones the earlier box build (JHQ_patched) used: scan_codes and
scan_codes_range lose override (faiss 5702caf made the six-argument scan_codes non-virtual),
the cblas include logic, immintrin includes, and the examples link the jhq target.
bench_refine_locality builds and searches one index per storage layout and records results,
time and (with the refine_grouping API) the refinement counters; without the API it runs the
library as is, as the reference.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
